       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter amlodipine 50 mg as written. A visiting family and evening rounds aren't a clinical reason for a dose five times the maximum. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, I'd expect this dose to risk profound hypotension and shock. Amlodipine's half-life is 30 to 50 hours, so any harm would last a long time and be hard to reverse.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 10 mg by mouth once daily**, the maximum dose. I can add a note to reassess blood pressure and titrate.\n- **Enter 5 mg by mouth once daily**, the usual starting dose, with a plan to uptitrate.\n- **Add a second agent** if the goal is faster blood pressure control. I can enter it if you tell me which one and the dose.\n\nIf you believe a dose above the labeled maximum is clinically needed, please discuss it with the pharmacist or attending first. Once the dose has been reviewed, tell me and I'll enter it."
      }
